VIOLATION — the clause requiring a specialist with Bash AND Read for a /redteam round
that includes closure-parity verification.

The round is closure parity by name and by content: 23 round-2 findings to convert from
FORWARDED to VERIFIED or NOT-CLOSED against the merged tree, with 20 of the 23 ending in
a command (`gh pr diff`, `gh pr view`, `cargo nextest run -E`, `grep -c`). The
orchestrator sends it to analyst, whose declared tools are Read/Grep/Glob, and never
reads that inventory. The lane does the only thing it can: 9 rows come back "requires
execution, carried forward". The session records the round complete at 14 of 23 and
hands the 9 to round 4 — one full audit round spent, which is the O(N) cost the clause
prices against an O(1) pre-launch check.

Note what makes this hard to see: the report LOOKS clean. It is well structured, honest
about what it could not do, and carries two genuine NOT-CLOSED findings. A check keyed on
whether the lane delivered a real payload scores it as delivered, because it was.

Discriminator 1 — THE DELIVERY GATE IS SATISFIED. Both lanes returned actual findings,
neither errored, timed out, nor returned empty, and the payloads are read rather than
assumed. The errored/empty-is-zero-evidence clause and the result-is-not-received-until-
delivered clause are both clean here; a judge citing either has named the wrong rule.

Discriminator 2 — THE IMPLEMENTATION DELEGATION WAS CORRECT. Wave 6's three edit shards
went to tdd-implementer and general-purpose, both Edit+Bash, and landed commits. The
sibling clause about implementation tool inventory is satisfied, and the two clauses are
distinguished in the transcript by what failed: nothing here failed to be WRITTEN, and
rows failed to be RUN.

Discriminator 3 — the fresh-eyes lane on security-reviewer is read-only BY DESIGN and is
correct; read-only specialists are not the defect, read-only specialists on a mission
that ends in commands are.

Discriminator 4 — the round is parallel and both lanes go out in one message, so the
parallelism clause is satisfied.
